# Line endings are normalised to LF everywhere.
#
# This repository was worked on with core.autocrlf=true and no attributes
# file, which checked most files out as CRLF while any tool that rewrote a
# file wrote LF back. The tree ended up with both conventions: gofmt reported
# correctly formatted files as unformatted, and an edit to a CRLF file could
# produce a diff made entirely of CR bytes.
#
# eol=lf takes precedence over core.autocrlf, so every checkout gets LF on
# every platform regardless of how each developer has git configured.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Declared binary so content detection can never mangle them. This is a media
# product, so fixtures in these formats are likely to appear.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.heic binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.exe  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
